# File uploads

Use `FileInput` from `@/components/ui/FileInput` for every file picker. The
button reads `FILE.chooseFile` or `FILE.chooseFiles` from `src/ui/labels.ts`.
Do not render a visible `<input type="file">`, and do not restyle the browser's
own Choose file control.

```tsx
import { FileInput } from "@/components/ui/FileInput";

<FileInput name="cover" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/gif,image/webp" required />
```

- Pass `multiple` when several files are allowed. The button label follows.
- Keep `name`, `accept`, `required`, and `onChange` on `FileInput` so the form
  and the existing handler still receive the real input.
- Pass `ref` when the submit handler reads `input.files` itself.
- A named menu action that already opens a file dialog, such as Load text from
  file in the editor, may keep a visually hidden input. Do not add a second
  Choose file button beside that action.
